# PR description — plain English (hard rule)

**Every time** you create or edit a GitHub PR (`gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`), the body **must** be easy to understand for a human who did not write the code.

## Required sections (in order)

```markdown
## What this PR does (plain English)

<2–4 sentences: what changes, for whom, why. No jargon-only bullets.>

**This PR does not** <explicit non-goals>

## Hard rule (every PR)

> **One concern per PR and per commit.** Never mix docs + production code, or two different tasks, in the same PR.

This PR’s single concern: **`<one path or concern label>`**.

## Why it matters in iPix

<2–4 sentences: real product/ops consequence. Name a surface, persona, or workflow.>

## Test plan

- [ ] <concrete checks a reviewer can run>
```

## Real-world hooks (use what fits)

| Domain | Example |
|--------|---------|
| Operator chat | Production Planner shot list, refresh keeps history |
| Auth / data | Login → org-scoped thread; Org B cannot read Org A |
| Mastra | Planner tools stay compute-only until HITL RPC |
| Host | Split `dev:ui` / `dev:agent` — combined `npm run dev` stays blocked |

### Good vs bad

| ✅ Good | ❌ Bad |
|--------|--------|
| “After refresh, the operator still sees the SS26 shot-list chat instead of a blank thread.” | “Wire PostgresStore schemaName and disableInit.” |
| “Org B is denied the same CopilotKit threadId so tenants cannot leak planner history.” | “Fix resourceId partition key.” |

## Rules

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Lead with what / for whom / why | Lead with file lists only |
| Name the **single concern** | Bundle seed + E2E + docs as one PR |
| Full task names on first mention | Bare `IPI-488` |
| Keep the hard-rule block | Soften one-concern |

## Title

`IPI-NNN · TASK-ID — Plain English title` (see `task-naming.mdc`).
